        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- SESSION DETAILS -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>5. Session Details</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Answer practical questions before a prospective client contacts you.
    </p>

    <label class=""check-item"">
      <input type=""checkbox"">
      <span>
        <strong>Session length is specified</strong>
        <small>
          Let prospective clients know whether sessions are typically
          45, 50, 53, 60, or another number of minutes.
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class=""check-item"">
      <input type=""checkbox"">
      <span>
        <strong>Typical session frequency is explained</strong>
        <small>
          If appropriate, describe what the beginning of counseling
          typically looks like, such as weekly sessions.
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class=""check-item"">
      <input type=""checkbox"">
      <span>
        <strong>Accessibility information is provided</strong>
        <small>
          Include relevant information about parking, stairs,
          accessibility, or online-only services.
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- APPROACH -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>6. Approach & Counseling Style</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Help prospective clients understand what working with you may feel like.
    </p>

    <label class=""check-item"">
      <input type=""checkbox"">
      <span>
        <strong>Counseling approach is explained clearly</strong>
        <small>
          Briefly explain the approaches you use in language that
          prospective clients can understand.
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class=""check-item"">
      <input type=""checkbox"">
      <span>
        <strong>Your counseling style is consistent throughout</strong>
        <small>
          Make sure your headline, bio, and description of your approach
          communicate a consistent professional identity.
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class=""check-item"">
      <input type=""checkbox"">
      <span>
        <strong>Your values or professional philosophy are visible</strong>
        <small>
          Include a brief personal or professional perspective that
          helps prospective clients understand what matters to you.
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- PHOTO -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>7. Photo & Visual Presentation</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Make sure your visual presentation matches the professional experience
      you want prospective clients to expect.
    </p>

    <label class=""check-item"">
      <input type=""checkbox"">
      <span>
        <strong>Photo is recent</strong>
        <small>
          Use a photo that reasonably reflects your current appearance.
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class=""check-item"">
      <input type=""checkbox"">
      <span>
        <strong>Background is clean and uncluttered</strong>
        <small>
          Keep visual distractions to a minimum so attention stays
          on you.
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class=""check-item"">
      <input type=""checkbox"">
      <span>
        <strong>Lighting is clear and natural</strong>
        <small>
          Use even lighting without distracting shadows or harsh
          contrast.
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class=""check-item"">
      <input type=""checkbox"">
      <span>
        <strong>Expression feels approachable</strong>
        <small>
          Choose an image that feels authentic to your personality
          and professional style.
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

  </div>


  <div class=""completion-box"" id=""completionBox"">

    <div class=""completion-title"">
      Profile checklist complete
    </div>

    <div class=""completion-text"">
      Your profile has been reviewed across all major sections.
